# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project following the official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` package using npm with `--legacy-peer-deps` flag
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the dependency tree

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified: `app/layout.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component in the body alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component
- The component is placed at the end of the body tag as recommended by Vercel documentation

## Implementation Details

This is a Next.js 16 project using the App Router pattern. Following the official Vercel documentation for Next.js v13.5+, I:

1. Imported the `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next` (the Next.js-specific export)
2. Added the component to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`)
3. Placed it alongside the existing Vercel Analytics component for consistency

The implementation follows Next.js best practices and the project's existing patterns, where Vercel Analytics was already configured in the same location.

## Notes

- The project had peer dependency conflicts due to the beta version of Prisma packages being used, so installation required the `--legacy-peer-deps` flag
- The Speed Insights component is now ready to collect performance metrics when the application is deployed to Vercel
- No breaking changes were made to existing functionality
- The component integrates seamlessly with the existing Clerk authentication and Vercel Analytics setup

## Testing

- Verified that the TypeScript import syntax is correct
- Confirmed the component is properly placed in the layout hierarchy
- Ensured the changes follow the existing code structure and patterns

The Speed Insights will automatically start collecting data once the application is deployed to Vercel.
